    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d792">

                <pb facs="0916" n="904" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg904"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811B.001 Quezon, Manuel/168</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of Staff</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Marshall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-04-20">April 20, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: The President has approved
                    the plans for the return of Mr. Quezon as outlined in the attached paper.
                    However, he directed that you be contacted reference same.</p>
                <pb facs="0917" n="905" xml:id="pg905"/>
                <p>Your concurrence is requested.<anchor n="52" xml:id="d792-f1"/></p>
                <closer>For the Chief of Staff:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dwight D.
                            Eisenhower</hi></signed>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Major General,
                        Assistant Chief of Staff</hi></closer>


                <xi:include href="d792-a1.xml" xpointer="d792-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d792-f1" n="52" xml:id="d792-f1-content">
                <p>An attached undated chit by Mr. Welles states that concurrence was given.
                    President Quezon, four members of his family, Vice President Osmeña, and an
                    entourage of 13 sailed from Australia on April 21 and arrived at San Francisco
                    on May 8.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
